SUMMARY: Mesh-LLM & Trusting a Stranger's Machine\, Part 2: Evidence You C
 an Check
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nWhen a stranger's machine serves an AI r
 equest\, how can the requester check what happened? We'll show mesh-llm's 
 Evidence plugin recording signed\, hash-chained evidence on each node and 
 sending each side's signed record to the other.\n\nA demo build will show 
 both-sides confirmation and a paid Lightning exchange\; we'll label the bu
 ild and distinguish it from a released version. I'll show a TRACE record a
 longside the exchange capsule to explain what additional runtime evidence\
 , including hardware evidence when available\, can establish. We'll also s
 how the limits: the plugin's node keys are self-attested\, and its referee
  applies once mesh-llm marks twins.
